  "notes": {
    "raw": "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 7 8 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 1 0. 2 9 0 + 4. 8 4 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 0. 3 3 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {5} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 2} \\\\ \\mathrm{H} ^ {\\circ} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {\\circ} = 1 0. 2 9 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 2. 4 2 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 0. 3 3 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} - 3. 3 9 4 \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 7 8 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 2 9. 0 4 2 + 0. 7 9 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 1. 4 5 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 5. 8 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 2 9. 0 4 2 - 0. 7 9 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} - 1. 4 5 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 2. 9 2 5 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 2 5. 3 7 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Stuve (112). Other data from Ferrante (37). ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
